WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.894
The words can be right, but the voice can still feel wrong for the moment.

00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:14.802
Interactive TTS adapts how an assistant speaks to the situation. Let's see three

00:00:14.802 --> 00:00:15.295
examples.

00:00:16.675 --> 00:00:22.651
First, watch this quiet-room interaction. Notice the cue for a softer reply.

00:00:36.967 --> 00:00:41.311
Now listen to the generated reply. It stays soft and gentle.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.474
The weather looks good this weekend.

00:00:44.474 --> 00:00:47.814
We could visit a nearby wetland park.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:51.155
It's quiet and uncrowded, just right for relaxing.

00:00:53.342 --> 00:00:58.838
Next, a train is arriving. The assistant needs to be heard over the noise.

00:01:10.175 --> 00:01:15.143
The generated reply uses a louder voice and a slightly faster pace.

00:01:16.508 --> 00:01:19.058
The next train to the airport arrives in four minutes.

00:01:19.058 --> 00:01:20.758
Take exit B when you arrive.

00:01:20.758 --> 00:01:23.308
Turn right after the gates for the airport bus stop.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:31.539
Here, the user is sharing good news. Notice the emotion before you hear the response.

00:01:42.883 --> 00:01:47.227
The reply becomes warm and happy, matching the moment.

00:01:48.592 --> 00:01:50.736
That's wonderful, I'm so happy for you!

00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:55.024
Your hard work brought you here. You deserve it.

00:01:55.024 --> 00:01:59.312
Celebrate; you've waited so long for this day.

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:07.227
These are separate scenarios. The task is to infer how to speak from the interaction.

00:02:08.967 --> 00:02:15.387
Our system first turns the context into an explicit speaking instruction: for example,

00:02:15.387 --> 00:02:18.351
low volume and a gentle tone.

00:02:19.717 --> 00:02:25.065
The speech generator follows that instruction to say the reply, using a reference

00:02:25.065 --> 00:02:25.477
voice.

00:02:26.842 --> 00:02:32.737
Across dialogue turns, the instruction can change. The same reference voice is reused

00:02:32.737 --> 00:02:35.458
to help keep the speaker consistent.

00:02:36.842 --> 00:02:42.773
Training teaches the instruction model to read the situation, and the speech model to

00:02:42.773 --> 00:02:46.586
follow style, preserve the voice, and fit the context.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:54.936
Interactive TTS. Understand the situation. Adapt the expression. Explore the full demo

00:02:54.936 --> 00:02:56.679
for more examples.
